# EvaluateCondition.srv
#
# One consolidated service covering every problog_project Condition node
# EXCEPT HaltedWith -- DistanceBelow/Equal/Over, ObstacleInBound/OnPath,
# BatteryBelow/Equal/Over, LineOfSightClear (see
# problog_project/module/contracts/schema.yaml for each one's own
# semantics). Same "one node, several functors sharing one shape" idea
# schema.yaml itself groups these nine under, and the same consolidation
# PlanPath.srv already applies to the four planning algorithms.
#
# HaltedWith is deliberately NOT covered here: it asks whether a
# PREVIOUS leg/planning call in THIS TREE's own history ended with a
# given reason, which is blackboard/tree-local state this service has
# no access to -- not something a stateless ROS service can answer, and
# something a future BT.cpp HaltedWith node should instead implement by
# reading its own tree's blackboard directly.
#
# Server: amiga_ros2_planners' condition_service_node. Every check reads
# the robot's CURRENT state at call time (tf2 pose, the orchard's own
# tree list, the simulated battery topic) -- see that node's own module
# docstring for exactly where each condition's inputs come from.

# One of: "DistanceBelow", "DistanceEqual", "DistanceOver",
# "ObstacleInBound", "ObstacleOnPath", "BatteryBelow", "BatteryEqual",
# "BatteryOver", "LineOfSightClear", "SampleValueBelow", "SampleValueEqual",
# "SampleValueOver", "CollisionDetected", "Hitched", "Deployed",
# "PloughedAt", "PloughedBetween" -- selects which fields below are
# actually used, mirroring each condition's own ports in schema.yaml.
string condition

# Distance* / LineOfSightClear: the point to check against, world/map
# frame metres. PloughedAt/PloughedBetween: the point (PloughedAt) or
# FIRST point (PloughedBetween's own p1) to check, same field reused --
# both are just "a point", and PloughedBetween needs a second one
# (p2_x/p2_y, below). Unused by Obstacle*/Battery*/SampleValue*/Hitched/
# Deployed.
float64 goal_x
float64 goal_y

# PloughedBetween only: the SECOND point (p2) of the swath to check --
# see goal_x/goal_y above for the first (p1). Unused by every other
# condition.
float64 p2_x
float64 p2_y

# Distance* / ObstacleInBound / ObstacleOnPath: metres.
# Battery*: percent, 0-100.
# SampleValue*: the drawn value threshold, 0-10.
float64 threshold

# LineOfSightClear: which tree to check occlusion against. Matches
# orchard_obstacles.py's "tree_<tree_index>" id convention.
string obstacle_id

# SampleValue*: must match the id= of an earlier <TakeSample> in this
# tree. Looked up against condition_service_node's own cache of
# sample_service_node's latched sample-values topic -- see that node's
# own module docstring. Unused by every other condition.
string sample_id

# CollisionDetected: one of "front", "back", "left", "right" (a specific
# chassis bumper contact sensor -- amiga_ros2_gazebo/models/amiga_kinova/
# model.sdf's own chassis_contact_<side>) or "any" (true if ANY side is
# currently in contact). Unused by every other condition.
string side

# Hitched: "cart", "plow", or empty/omitted to check "is ANYTHING
# currently attached" instead of one specific kind -- matches
# schema.yaml's own Hitched.kind (optional). Unused by every other
# condition.
string kind

---
# Response

# The condition's truth value.
bool result

# Empty on an ordinary result. Set only when `result` is false because
# the check itself could not be performed (e.g. no tf2 pose yet, no
# battery reading yet, or obstacle_id names no known tree) rather than
# because the condition was genuinely false -- so a caller that needs to
# tell "false" from "couldn't tell" can.
string reason
